attention-softmax shifts by the max before exponentiating, so
every argument it passes attn-exp is at or below zero:
  attn-exp 0 = 1000  true 1000 exact, the control: no truncation can move it
  attn-exp -1000 = 367  true 368
  attn-exp -2000 = 135  true 135
  attn-exp -3000 = 49  true 50
  attn-exp -4000 = 18  true 18
  attn-exp -5000 = 6  true 7

samp-exp, which samp-cand-exp asks the same way:
  samp-exp 0 = 1000  true 1000 exact, the control
  samp-exp -1000 = 367  true 368
  samp-exp -2000 = 135  true 135
  samp-exp -3000 = 49  true 50
  samp-exp -4000 = 18  true 18

dpmpp-exp, asked for exp(-h) by both DPM++ orders, and
flux-exp-approx, which flux-pow asks on the positive side:
  dpmpp-exp 0 = 1000  true 1000 exact, the control
  dpmpp-exp -2000 = 135  true 135
  dpmpp-exp -3000 = 49  true 50
  dpmpp-exp 2000 = 7387  true 7389
  dpmpp-exp 8000 = 2978115  true 2980958, at the top of its own guarded range
  flux-exp -2000 = 135  true 135
  flux-exp 2000 = 7387  true 7389

emb-exp-range reduces by 693, which is ln 2 at this scale. It
was already correct and is untouched, so it is the control:
  emb-exp 0 = 1000  true 1000 exact, the control
  emb-exp 693 = 2000  true 2000
  emb-exp 2303 = 10000  true 10000
  emb-exp 4605 = 99840  true 100000
  emb-exp 9210 = 10010624  true 10000000

Counted rather than eyeballed. exp is strictly decreasing on
the negative axis and never negative, so a correct row reads
13 of 13 for each of the first three and 14 of 14 for emb:
  attn-exp non-increasing over z=0..-6:  13 of 13
  samp-exp non-increasing over z=0..-6:  13 of 13
  dpmpp-exp non-increasing over z=0..-6: 13 of 13
  attn-exp non-negative over z=0..-6:    13 of 13
  samp-exp non-negative over z=0..-6:    13 of 13
  emb-exp-range non-decreasing 0..9100:  14 of 14

Positional encoding, at dim 8 where the divisor for d=0 is 1 so
the argument is the raw position. Even d is sin, odd d is cos:
  pos-enc-value pos=1 d=0 dim=8 1 = 841  true 841, sin 1
  pos-enc-value pos=2 d=0 dim=8 2 = 908  true 909, sin 2
  pos-enc-value pos=4 d=0 dim=8 4 = -756  true -757, sin 4, and it needed both fixes
  pos-enc-value pos=1 d=1 dim=8 1 = 538  true 540, cos 1

One row still asserts nothing and says so: at d=6 the divisor is
1000, so the true value is sin 0.001 = 0.001, which is one unit
at this scale and reads 0. That is the bottom of the fixed point,
not the scale defect, and no fix here can move it:
  pos-enc-value pos=1 d=6 dim=8 1 = 0  true 1, and 0 is the representable floor
